            <ArticleTitle>Radiology Of The Month: Spontaneous Bilateral Pneumothoraces in an HIV-Infected Patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>120-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 36-year-old woman with past medical history of HIV/AIDS not on HAART therapy (CD4 count of 34) and recurrent Pneumocystis jiroveci pneumonia presented to the emergency room for cough, chest pain, and worsening shortness of breath over the past 72 hours.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
